🔁 git rebase
✅ What It Does:
rebase moves or reapplies a series of commits from one branch onto another base.

🔍 Use Case:
When you want to make your feature branch look like it was based off the latest main branch (i.e., clean, linear history).

🧪 Example:
bash
Copy
Edit
# Suppose you're on 'feature' and want to rebase onto 'main'
git checkout feature
git rebase main
This means:

"Take all commits from feature, and replay them on top of the latest main."


git reset:
| Command             | What it Resets             | Working Dir | Use Case                                 |
| ------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `git reset --soft`  | HEAD only                  | ✅ Keeps     | Undo commit, keep staged                 |
| `git reset --mixed` | HEAD + Index (default)     | ✅ Keeps     | Uncommit + unstage, but keep changes     |
| `git reset --hard`  | HEAD + Index + Working Dir | ❌ Discards  | Completely undo commit + code changes ⚠️ |
